@romseygeek Please check my recent changes- I tried to find the best combination of code reuse for `XContentHelper#mergeDefaults` as well as safe refactor and zero overhead for existing usages of this legacy functionality. 

From all I can tell- it works as expected and solves the issue generically at all levels of the merged documents. Hopefully the full test suite will not uncover issues that I couldn't find manually.

I don't like the hard-coded distinction between object and non-object fields, but since I need to do that in the raw map form, I couldn't think of a better way. Let me know if you think it needs different handling.

